# Saku — Personal Finance Tracker
# Flutter + Clean Architecture + Local Storage (Hive)
# Minimalist Black & White iOS-style Design

---

## Project Overview

- App name: **Saku**
- Platform: Flutter (iOS & Android)
- Architecture: Clean Architecture
- Storage: Hive (local only, no backend)
- State Management: flutter_riverpod
- Navigation: go_router
- Design: Minimalist Black & White, iOS-style
- App Icon assets: ROOT_PROJECT/assets/app_icons
---

## Strict Coding Rules

- Always follow Clean Architecture: data → domain → presentation
- Never call Hive or any datasource directly from presentation layer
- Always go through use cases from providers/notifiers
- Never use colors other than: #000000, #FFFFFF, #F5F5F5, #1C1C1E, #8E8E93, #E0E0E0, #2C2C2E
- All monetary amounts stored as `int` in IDR (no decimals)
- Always use `formatRupiah()` from `core/utils/currency_formatter.dart` for display
- Always use `freezed` for domain entities
- Always use `const` constructors wherever possible
- Always handle loading and error states in UI
- Never hardcode strings — use constants or l10n
- New feature checklist: entity → repository (abstract) → repository (impl) → datasource → usecase → provider → UI

